meta {
  name: Respond (claim order)
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/master/orders/{{order_id}}/respond
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  X-Locale: {{locale}}
}

docs {
  # Respond — claim an offered order

  The master takes an order from the auto-search feed. This is a **race**: the
  same order is offered to every master in range, and the claim is settled by
  an atomic conditional update — whoever gets there first wins, the rest get
  `422 already claimed`.

  Everything is re-checked server-side, including the distance, because nothing
  stops an app from POSTing an order id it never received in the feed.

  On success the order becomes `assigned`, `MasterAssigned` is broadcast to the
  client's channel, and the response carries the full order **with** the
  client's contact details.

  **Response 200:** `MasterOrderResource` with `status: "assigned"`

  **Errors (all `422`, message localized by `X-Locale`):**

  | Cause                                    | Meaning                              |
  |------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------|
  | already claimed                          | another master won, or admin assigned |
  | search expired                           | auto-search gave up; admin assigns now |
  | category mismatch                        | not one of the master's trades        |
  | out of search radius                     | too far for the order's current radius |
  | master location unknown                  | no GPS ping yet                       |
  | master unavailable / access expired      | switched off, blocked, or unsubscribed |

  - `404` — order not found
  - `403` — token has no usable master profile (see `reason`)
}
